WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
-This show is based off a memoir

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
of an actual
medical director at Bellevue.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.073
-Did you read the book once you
found out about the role?

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, once I
found out about it --

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:11.678
I hadn't heard of the book when
I was auditioning for the --

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we were talking about
doing the show.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was one of the things
that drew me to it,

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that it was based on,
you know,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
Eric's real experiences
in this hospital

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.522
with real people, real patients,
that it was gonna be about

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:25.258
healthcare, you know, from very
specific source material.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:28.094
-And now he's a producer on the
show and will stop by set.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does he give any advice on how
to be a better fake doctor?

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nobody does fake doctor
like me.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. He --
He does.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.773 size:78% position:39%
He really, you know,
runs quality control,

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
keeps us honest,
and makes sure that we're,

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.143 line:92%
A, telling the right stories.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, he provides
a lot of ideas for sort of

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:48.148
real things that he experienced,
and then, yeah, makes sure

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:51.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're -- that we're doing
it as honestly as we can.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.821 size:84% position:42%
-You come by playing
a fake doctor honestly.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your parents are real doctors.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have a sister
who's a nurse?

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did this ever appeal to you
as a real path to take?

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Okay.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First off,
my family's got it covered.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:07.934 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah, they really do.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My sister's an amazing nurse,
and my folks are the best.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would be just
a terrible doctor.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:13.907 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Why do you think --

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also think
I'd be a terrible doctor,

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
but why do you think you'd be
a terrible doctor?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just can't --
I mean, we'll be at work,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:22.182 size:78% position:39%
and they'll be doing
a fake surgery scene.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hopefully
not a real surgery scene.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, they'll play
video of a heartbeat,

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.591 size:88% position:44%
and I just can't even --
I can't even look at it.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will immediately just --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.396 size:78% position:39%
It'll come from here
and all over the set.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's a real bad sign.
Yeah.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It's not a bad move.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
Honestly, it's just another
expense to just clean that up.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you actually shoot
in real hospitals.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.175
And people --
So you're dressed for the part.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.212
Do people ever mistake you
for a doctor, a real doctor?

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:56.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's my biggest fear,
and sometimes it does happen.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like when we were doing
the pilot --

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
We shoot in real hospitals
all the time --

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:02.422
Kings County, Bellevue, and,
you know, you're in scrubs.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.223 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And people have no idea.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
And someone will come up
and, you know --

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Uh, this way."
I just point and be like,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
Go -- I can't help."
-Yeah.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.297
Well, the funny thing is,
if somebody ran in and is like,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.834
"Is there a doctor here?!"
and you're dressed as a doctor,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.768 line:92%
if you were like, "No"...

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they look at you,
and you go...

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you just look like
a really cowardly doctor.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just, like, a jerk.
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just sitting next to you,
bleeding, going,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.644 size:78% position:39%
"Sorry, man, I can't.
-"It's not my thing.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not my thing."
-Can't help you with that.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have
a catch phrase on the show.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you using it
in your real life?

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I mean,
it's a great catch phrase,

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it ends up making its way
into my life --

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
anybody's life.
It's, "How can I help?"

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
is what my character says.
And I was on a plane.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.393
I was flying back to New York,
and this woman was struggling,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
putting a stroller
up in the overhead bin.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just said,
"How can I help?"

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:48.001
And a few people kind of looked,
like, "Dude, you're not on TV.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Relax."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We get it.
We've seen the show.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just help..."
"Sorry."

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah.
-Yeah whenever --

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.610
I do it, too, whenever my kids
are like, "Daddy, what's this?"

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.846
I'm like,
"It's time for 'A Closer Look.'"

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
You --
I want to ask --

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like, "We're over it."
They're over it.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Big eye-roll.
-So, well, I want to start --

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.291
So, I've seen these, of course,
on the subway, as well.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.625
So, first of all, this is great,
'cause this --

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
First, I want to show
the "New Amsterdam" poster.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.096
But a lot of people on Instagram
have pointed out

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.632
it looks like you're telling
them about the other poster.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, they're like,

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, go see Blue Man Group."
-In addition

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.739
to playing a doctor, I also play
a New York City tour guide.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm just pointing
at stuff to do.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and we should say,
your show's great,

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.278
but also, you obviously want us
to watch Amy Sedaris over there.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.814
-It's a great cake.
Yeah, it's a good-looking cake.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.016 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Some of your co-stars,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've really enjoyed
mocking you.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:41.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everybody, yes.
As often as they can.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
She does it better than I do.
-She does it better.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.992
Topher Grace, one of your
"BlacKkKlansman" co-stars.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.861 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, he's auditioning
for the role, as well.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the best one, though,
because when you're in

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:55.168
New York City, you really want
someone to put graffiti on it.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:55.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.237
-This person
didn't even care about the hand.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody else
was drawn to the hand.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:01.641
-This is how you know
that you're really hitting home

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the core message...
-Yeah.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...of putting the care
back in healthcare.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
And I think that's true.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:09.282
You've talked about this show.
This is a doctor with integrity.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:09.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:13.152
-And this graffiti artist
obviously appreciated that.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This really
just kind of says it all.

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Dis bitch."
-"Dis bitch."

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you can see that there.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
As you can see.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is how New York
lets you know.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.531 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's how they let you know.
-They love me.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.502 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's New York.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:32.171 size:81% position:41%
I've seen other things
drawn on my forehead.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
I won't say exactly what.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:35.174 size:81% position:41%
-Pretty much anything,
yeah, graffiti-wise.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But that's really nice.
It is -- that makes me laugh

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
so hard when someone sees that
and is like, "I got it."

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:45.351
-Real-life meme
just on your poster right there.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, well,
congratulations on the show

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.955 line:92%
and everything else this year.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
The film is great,
and the show is great.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thanks so much
for being here.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.359 line:92%
-Thanks for having me, brother.

